// The `windows_subsystem = "windows"` attribute lives on the binaries that embed
// this library, since the subsystem is a link-time property. On Windows
// `aterm.exe` is console-subsystem (the shell waits for every verb) and
// `aterm-gui.exe` (the `aterm-windowed` bin) is windowed. `main_entry` first calls
// `win32::attach_parent_console` so `--help`/`--version` print to a launching
// console, and releases that console once it decides to open a window.

//! `aterm-gui` — the native windowed aterm terminal.
//!
//! A winit window presenting the `aterm-render` framebuffer over a shell in a PTY.
//! Background threads read the PTYs and feed the engine; the main thread runs the
//! event loop, rasterizes the grid and handles input.
// A tree mutation (`remove_leaf(`, `split_leaf(`, …) riding inside a
// `debug_assert!` vanishes from a release build: the lint refuses the shape
// wherever it is written, instead of a test grepping three files for it.
#![deny(clippy::debug_assert_with_mut_call)]
#![cfg_attr(
    test,
    allow(
        clippy::disallowed_types,
        reason = "test code: a stand-in child may inherit descriptors"
    )
)]

